# Line-ending policy.
#
# Go sources are stored and checked out with LF on every platform. Without this,
# a developer with `core.autocrlf=true` (the default on Windows Git) gets CRLF in
# the working tree, and `gofmt -l` then reports 22 otherwise-correctly-formatted
# files as unformatted — emitting a full-file diff for each one. Normalising here
# makes the CI `gofmt` check mean the same thing on every machine.
* text=auto
*.go text eol=lf
